{"additions":5355,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nCloses #170.\n\n- **`core::gh_fixture`** — with `VIG_GH_FIXTURE=<dir>` (recording-only, undocumented for users, same standing as `VIG_PROCS_ROOT_PID`) every `gh` invocation in `run_gh` returns the file named after its arguments from `<dir>` instead of running `gh`; a missing file is a loud error so a demo never half-works, `gh auth status` passes when the directory exists, and the disk caches are bypassed so a recording always starts from the fixture state. GraphQL query text is replaced by a short tag in the file name (`query-project-meta`, `query-pr-stacks`, …); everything else is sanitised and deterministic.\n- **`vig fixtures record <dir>`** (hidden subcommand, `src/fixtures.rs`) runs the GitHub and Projects pages' real commands — issue / PR lists and details, PR stacks, runs plus the first three runs' jobs and logs, linked projects, the viewer login, each board over the GraphQL path and its items' details — teeing every response into `<dir>`. `mise run fixtures:refresh` wraps it and is the only step of the demo pipeline that touches the API. The whitespace pre-commit fixers skip `tape/fixtures/` so recordings stay byte-exact.\n- **Tapes** — `demo-github-issue`, `demo-github-pr` and `demo-projects` replay `tape/fixtures/` through `VIG_GH_FIXTURE` set by their mise tasks; `Require gh` and the cache-wiping line go away. `mise run demo:all` no longer needs the network or spends points.\n- **Integration tests** — `page_loads_a_board_from_recorded_fixtures` (Projects: linked projects → board via GraphQL → views, rendered with `TestBackend`) and `page_loads_lists_from_recorded_fixtures` (GitHub: issues and runs load and render) run against the same recordings, skipping when `tape/fixtures` is absent (packaged sources).\n- `CLAUDE.md`'s demo checklist explains the mechanism for contributors.\n\n## Demo\n\n`demo-github-issue.gif` and `demo-projects.gif` are re-recorded from the fixtures (same content, zero API calls). The PR demo follows in a commit on this branch: the fixtures are refreshed once this PR exists so the recorded PR list is not empty, then `demo-github-pr` is re-recorded from them.\n\n## Tests\n\nFixture naming / replay unit tests plus the two page-level integration tests. 394 tests green, clippy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":61,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-08T10:13:05Z","deletions":22,"headRefName":"feat/gh-fixtures","labels":[],"number":174,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMmSRCg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new fixture-driven integration tests and fixture recorder currently leave global fixture state enabled and ignore key recording errors, which can make tests nondeterministic and fixture refreshes incomplete.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR adds a record/replay mechanism for GitHub CLI (`gh`) output so demo GIF recording and page-level integration tests can run without network access or GitHub API quota usage, aligning the GitHub/Projects pages with deterministic, fixture-driven workflows.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduce `core::gh_fixture` to replay recorded `gh` responses (via `VIG_GH_FIXTURE`) and optionally record real `gh` stdout to fixture files.\n- Add a hidden `vig fixtures record <dir>` subcommand to generate/update fixture sets by running the GitHub and Projects pages’ `gh` queries against the current repo.\n- Update demo tapes/tasks to replay from `tape/fixtures`, and add integration tests that render pages using recorded fixtures.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161906_--log_--job_102018695599.out | Added recorded workflow job log fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161906_--log_--job_102018675438.out | Added recorded workflow job log fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161906_--log_--job_102018649318.out | Added recorded workflow job log fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161906_--json_jobs.out | Added recorded workflow jobs JSON fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161726_--json_jobs.out | Added recorded workflow jobs JSON fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161710_--log_--job_102018699684.out | Added recorded workflow job log fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161710_--log_--job_102018647351.out | Added recorded workflow job log fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161710_--json_jobs.out | Added recorded workflow jobs JSON fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_list_--limit_50_--json_databaseId_number_name_workflowName_status_conclusion_headBranch_event_createdAt_updatedAt_url.out | Added recorded workflow run list fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/repo_view_--json_nameWithOwner_owner_projectsV2.out | Added recorded repo metadata (linked projects) fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/repo_view_--json_nameWithOwner_-q_.nameWithOwner.out | Added recorded repo name fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/pr_list_--json_number_title_state_author_labels_headRefName_baseRefName_createdAt_reviewDecision_isDraft_--limit_50.out | Added recorded PR list fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_170_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Added recorded issue detail fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_123_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Added recorded issue detail fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_122_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Added recorded issue detail fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_121_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Added recorded issue detail fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_120_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Added recorded issue detail fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_119_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Added recorded issue detail fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_118_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Added recorded issue detail fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_114_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Added recorded issue detail fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_list_--json_number_title_state_author_labels_createdAt_parent_--limit_50.out | Added recorded issue list fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/auth_status.out | Added recorded `gh auth status` output (fixture presence marker). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_user_--jq_.login.out | Added recorded viewer login fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-meta_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2.out | Added recorded Projects GraphQL “meta” fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-items_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2_-F_first_8.out | Added recorded Projects GraphQL “items” fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-pr-stacks_-F_owner_td72_-F_name_vig_-F_first_50.out | Added recorded PR stacks GraphQL fixture for replay. |\r\n| tape/demo-projects.tape | Switch Projects demo tape to fixture replay (remove `Require gh` and cache wipe). |\r\n| tape/demo-github-issue.tape | Switch GitHub issue demo tape to fixture replay (remove `Require gh`). |\r\n| src/projects/state.rs | Add fixture-driven Projects page integration test rendering via `TestBackend`. |\r\n| src/main.rs | Add hidden `fixtures` subcommand wiring to record fixtures. |\r\n| src/github/state.rs | Add fixture-driven GitHub page integration test rendering via `TestBackend`. |\r\n| src/github/domain/disk_cache.rs | Disable disk cache usage when fixture replay is active. |\r\n| src/github/domain/client.rs | Hook `run_gh` into fixture replay/record paths. |\r\n| src/fixtures.rs | Implement `vig fixtures record <dir>` to generate/update fixtures. |\r\n| src/core/mod.rs | Export the new `gh_fixture` module. |\r\n| src/core/gh_fixture.rs | Implement deterministic fixture naming plus replay/record plumbing. |\r\n| prek.toml | Exclude `tape/fixtures/` from whitespace fixers to keep byte-exact recordings. |\r\n| mise.toml | Run demos with `VIG_GH_FIXTURE=...` and add `fixtures:refresh` task. |\r\n| CLAUDE.md | Document fixture-based demo approach for contributors (non-user-facing env var). |\r\n| assets/demo-projects.gif | Re-record Projects demo GIF (LFS pointer updated). |\r\n| assets/demo-github-issue.gif | Re-record GitHub Issue demo GIF (LFS pointer updated). |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**src/fixtures.rs:44**\n* This ignores failures when recording job logs. If a log fetch fails, replay mode will later hit a missing fixture and error during a demo or integration test. Propagate the error so fixture recording is complete and deterministic.\n```\n        let jobs = actions::list_jobs(run.id).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n        for job in &jobs {\n            let _ = actions::fetch_job_log(run.id, job.id, false);\n        }\n```\n**src/fixtures.rs:50**\n* This discards the viewer login fetch entirely, but the replay path expects a corresponding fixture for `gh api user --jq .login`. If it fails during recording, the missing fixture will later break demos/tests. Treat it as required here and return an error when unavailable.\n```\n    let info = projects::repo_info().map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n    let _ = projects::viewer_login();\n    for project in info.linked_projects() {\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 45/51 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T10:17:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"ba2786add22e6608d1e22dac38fe516700a24452"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMmVfnA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new fixture recorder and integration tests have a few confirmed reliability issues (ignored recording errors and global fixture state leaking across parallel tests) that should be addressed to avoid flaky CI and incomplete fixture generation.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (3)\n\n**src/fixtures.rs:35**\n* `gh::list_pr_stacks(50)` errors are currently ignored. If the GraphQL call fails during recording, the PR stacks fixture won’t be written and replay will error later (the whole point of `fixtures record` is to ensure fixtures exist). Consider propagating the error so the recording fails loudly.\n```\n    step(\"pull requests + stacks\");\n    let prs = gh::list_prs(50).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n    let _ = gh::list_pr_stacks(50);\n    for p in &prs {\n```\n**src/projects/state.rs:866**\n* This test sets a global fixture replay directory (`gh_fixture::set_replay_dir`) but never resets it. Rust tests run in parallel by default, so this can leak state into other tests and cause non-deterministic failures. Add a small guard to reset the replay dir on drop.\n```\n        let Some(dir) = crate::core::gh_fixture::recorded_dir() else {\n            return;\n        };\n        crate::core::gh_fixture::set_replay_dir(Some(dir));\n        let mut st = ProjectsState::new(&Config::builtin()).expect(\"projects page\");\n```\n**src/github/state.rs:1206**\n* This test sets a global fixture replay directory (`gh_fixture::set_replay_dir`) but never resets it. With parallel test execution, that can affect unrelated tests that use `run_gh` and introduce flakiness. Add a drop guard to restore the previous state (at least reset to `None`).\n```\n        let Some(dir) = crate::core::gh_fixture::recorded_dir() else {\n            return;\n        };\n        crate::core::gh_fixture::set_replay_dir(Some(dir));\n        let mut st = GitHubState::new(&Config::builtin()).expect(\"github page\");\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 45/51 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T10:22:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"1c330b2403a476484b3f4c05551a8cba0a8a9891"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMmZ19Q","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:34Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"1c330b2403a476484b3f4c05551a8cba0a8a9891"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMmZ3Og","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"dfd013d2b1b2cb4218af6336cd6d1b427bbc9f1a"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMmZ4Tw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"dfd013d2b1b2cb4218af6336cd6d1b427bbc9f1a"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMmZ5XA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"dfd013d2b1b2cb4218af6336cd6d1b427bbc9f1a"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMmdQiw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe fixture recorder currently discards several recording failures (and can be accidentally run with replay enabled), which can produce incomplete fixture sets and undermine deterministic demos/tests.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**src/fixtures.rs:35**\n* The PR stacks GraphQL call is currently ignored. If it fails during recording, the stacks fixture won’t be written and replay will silently fall back to a flat PR list, which makes fixture refreshes nondeterministic. At least warn when this fetch fails (or propagate the error).\n```\n    step(\"pull requests + stacks\");\n    let prs = gh::list_prs(50).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n    let _ = gh::list_pr_stacks(50);\n    for p in &prs {\n```\n**src/fixtures.rs:70**\n* Failures to record issue/PR details for project items are currently discarded (`let _ = …`). If any of these calls fail (permissions, transient API errors, etc.), replay will later be missing item detail fixtures without any indication during recording. Capture and report these errors (similar to `missing_logs`).\n```\n            let repo = item.repository().filter(|r| !r.eq_ignore_ascii_case(&nwo));\n            let _ = match item.kind() {\n                crate::projects::domain::types::ItemKind::Issue => {\n                    gh::get_issue_in(repo, number).map(|_| ())\n                }\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 49/61 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-09-08T10:35:31Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"dfd013d2b1b2cb4218af6336cd6d1b427bbc9f1a"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T13:03:44Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34229674291/job/102072420270","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-09-08T13:03:54Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T10:31:04Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34215732817/job/102026909690","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:40Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T10:30:18Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34215732833/job/102026909609","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:40Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T10:30:51Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34215732817/job/102026910090","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:42Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T10:31:45Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34215732817/job/102026909911","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:47Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T10:31:45Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34215732817/job/102027534109","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-09-08T10:31:46Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T13:03:44Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34229674291/job/102072372113","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-09-08T13:03:45Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T10:30:50Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34215732833/job/102026909891","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:40Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T10:31:39Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34215732833/job/102026909878","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-08T10:29:47Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-08T13:03:44Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34229674291/job/102072371202","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-09-08T13:03:45Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"🧪 Record and replay gh output for API-free demos and integration tests"}
